Below is the graph of $y = a \sin (bx + c) + d$ for some positive constants $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ and $d.$  Find $b.$

[asy]import TrigMacros;

size(400);

real f(real x)
{
	return 2*sin(3*x + pi) + 1;
}

draw(graph(f,-3*pi,3*pi,n=700,join=operator ..),red);
trig_axes(-3*pi,3*pi,-4,4,pi/2,1);
layer();
rm_trig_labels(-5,5, 2);

label("$1$", (0,1), E);
label("$2$", (0,2), E);
label("$3$", (0,3), E);
label("$-1$", (0,-1), E);
label("$-2$", (0,-2), E);
label("$-3$", (0,-3), E);
[/asy]

Let $P$ be the point on line segment $\overline{AB}$ such that $AP:PB = 2:7.$  Then
\[\overrightarrow{P} = t \overrightarrow{A} + u \overrightarrow{B}\]for some constants $t$ and $u.$  Enter the ordered pair $(t,u).$

[asy]
unitsize(1 cm);

pair A, B, P;

A = (0,0);
B = (5,1);
P = interp(A,B,2/9);

draw(A--B);

dot("$A$", A, S);
dot("$B$", B, S);
dot("$P$", P, S);
[/asy]

